{#
Renders a monthly trend as a horizontally-scrolling strip of compact cards (scan left to
right across months) instead of a tall vertical table you have to scroll down through.
`months` is an array of { month, count, alertCount?, analysisCount? }, at most one of
which is set per series. alertCount is Re-Entry's real MSH-reported monthly figure.
analysisCount is Collision & Fragmentation's month-bucketed "events past the analysis
threshold" count, a dashboard-computed approximation rather than an MSH-reported figure
(see tech-docs "Open questions") — shown as "needing analysis" rather than "alerts" so
it's not mistaken for the same kind of number. Fragmentation's trend has neither.
#}
{% macro monthStrip(months) %}
  <div class="msh-month-strip">
    {% for month in months %}
      <div class="msh-month-strip__card">
        <span class="msh-month-strip__label">{{ month.month }}</span>
        <span class="msh-month-strip__value">{{ month.count }}</span>
        {% if month.alertCount is defined %}
          <span class="msh-month-strip__sub">{{ month.alertCount }} alert{{ "s" if month.alertCount != 1 }}</span>
        {% elif month.analysisCount is defined %}
          <span class="msh-month-strip__sub">{{ month.analysisCount }} needing analysis</span>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
{% endmacro %}
